# SABOTAGE: MG-15 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — `Samen.Vault.Change.ensure_subject_attr/2`'s
# cond FALLTHROUGH is made unreachable (`true ->` → `false ->`). That arm is the one that
# FORCES the generated subject onto the row when the primary key is not yet set, so the
# ciphertext and the domain row share a subject. With every arm falsifiable the `cond`
# raises `CondClauseError` and the vaulted write dies inside the action instead.
#
# The shape that reaches it is the DB-generated-pk one the function's own comment names
# ("On create it may be unset (DB default gen_random_uuid())"): a create whose changeset
# carries no non-nil pk change and whose data has no pk. A resource taking the
# `Samen.Resource` default (`default: &Ash.UUID.generate/0`) short-circuits on the clause
# above instead, which is why every other create in the suite stays green under this flip —
# and why this red has to construct the unset-pk changeset explicitly.
#
# Flips the named MG-15 red. Every other test in that file stays green, so the red fails
# because the fallthrough is gone, not because vault routing, the subject resolver or the
# repo chain broke.
#
# One boolean literal on one cond clause. Touches vault/change.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/vault_change_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-15: a CREATE whose pk is UNSET still vaults (the fallthrough forces the subject)
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Vault.Change do
       match?({:ok, v} when not is_nil(v), Ash.Changeset.fetch_change(changeset, pk)) ->
         changeset
 
-      true ->
+      false ->
         Ash.Changeset.force_change_attribute(changeset, pk, subject_id)
     end
   end
